    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0129" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg33"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Herdliska</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 115, of the 4th ultimo, reporting your action in bringing to the
                    notice of the Austro-Hungarian Government the statement that if any of their
                    wounded required aid in Chinese waters they would be welcomed aboard the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, and that every possible assistance would be
                    given them by the ladies of the executive committee of the vessel.</p>
                <p>You are instructed, when a suitable occasion shall be offered, to express this
                    Government’s high appreciation of the action of the executive committee in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
